VERDICT: PASS -- EAP-Notification IS supported.  The DUT passes an
         EAP-Request/Notification from the RADIUS server to the supplicant, passes the
         supplicant's reply back to the server, and the authentication then continues
         normally.  The authored objective "Not Support" does not match the device.
      control, server sends no notification .... 6 EAPOL frames, no notification at
                                                 all, EAP-Success in 1.03 s
      same leg, server sends a notification .... 8 EAPOL frames; the two extra frames
                                                 are the Notification and its reply
      the text is not changed .................. 50 bytes in, 50 bytes out, the raw
                                                 bytes decode to the exact string
      the reply travels back to the server ..... the server logged
                                                 "EAP code=2(Response) type=Notification len=0"
      a notification decides nothing ........... good password EAP-Success 1.05 s,
                                                 bad password EAP-Failure 0.05 s, both
                                                 received the same notification
ALSO MEASURED:
      Setting `auth host-mode multi-supplicant` for leg C again changed
      `dot1x control-direction both` to `in` with no warning.  Proof after the steps.
CAVEAT:  The DUT writes nothing about the notification in its own log, so the switch
         log cannot be used as evidence for this feature.  Only the frames on the wire
         and the RADIUS server's own log can.  This run used one notification string of
         50 bytes.  It does not show what happens with a string long enough to need
         fragmenting, and it does not test a notification inside a TLS tunnel.
