TOPOLOGY AS TESTED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

   tb277 (the testbox) plays TWO roles in this case.

   role 1, supplicant                        role 2, RADIUS server
   eth4  00:0d:b9:55:77:0f                   eth3  10.38.22.33:11812
   source MACs 02:0d:b9:00:33:54 and :55     tools/radeap.py
            |                                        ^
            |  EAPOL                                 |  RADIUS/UDP, EAP-Message
            |  (ether proto 0x888e)                  |  with Message-Authenticator
            v                                        |
  +----------------------------------------------------------+
  |  swi_d  AT-x960-56YSQ                        * DUT *      |
  |                                                           |
  |  port1.0.48  vlan 48   <- the 802.1X controlled port      |
  |  port1.0.10  vlan 10   -> 10.38.22.34, the RADIUS path    |
  |  SVI MAC e0:1a:ea:d4:70:43                                |
  +----------------------------------------------------------+

  The RADIUS path deliberately uses the OTHER leg.  port1.0.48 is the port under test,
  so the DUT's own RADIUS traffic must not pass through it.

  DUT          : swi_d (AT-x960-56YSQ) console u2 at 115200, S/N A2WQS700B,
                 SVI MAC e0:1a:ea:d4:70:43, hostname awplus, not a stack
  supplicant   : tb277 eth4, tools/eapol.py, source MACs 02:0d:b9:00:33:54 and
                 02:0d:b9:00:33:55, identity cknotify
  auth server  : tb277 eth3 10.38.22.33 port 11812, tools/radeap.py, shared key
                 cknotify2026, user cknotify
  link, tested : tb277 eth4 <-> swi_d port1.0.48 (copper, untagged vlan 48)
  link, RADIUS : tb277 eth3 10.38.22.33/27 <-> swi_d port1.0.10, vlan 10, DUT 10.38.22.34
  tools        : tools/eapol.py and tools/radeap.py, both on tb277.  radeap.py was
                 started in the background BEFORE each supplicant call, because two
                 tool calls issued together run one after the other and a server
                 started beside the supplicant would not be listening yet.
                 tcpdump always filtered `ether proto 0x888e`.

STEP 0 -- point the DUT's 802.1X at the testbox's RADIUS server           done
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
awplus#configure terminal
awplus(config)#radius-server host 10.38.22.33 auth-port 11812 key cknotify2026
awplus(config)#aaa group server radius ckbox
awplus(config-sg)#server 10.38.22.33 auth-port 11812
awplus(config-sg)#exit
awplus(config)#aaa authentication dot1x default group ckbox
awplus(config)#exit
                                                 <-- `show radius` then listed both
                                                     127.0.0.1 port 1812 and
                                                     10.38.22.33 port 11812

  A named server group is used on purpose.  `group radius` would mean every configured
  RADIUS server, including the DUT's own local one.  A group with one member points
  only this case's 802.1X at the testbox, and one command removes it afterwards.
  Only the dot1x method list was changed.  The login method list was not touched.

STEP A -- control: the same exchange with NO notification                 PASS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Method: start the RADIUS server with no `--notify` flag, then run one supplicant.
  Nothing else differs from STEP B.

$ tools/tb tool tb277 dot1x1304 radeap --secret cknotify2026 --client 10.38.22.34 \
      --user cknotify:cknotifypw --auth-port 11812 --seconds 70 \
      --log /tmp/dot1x1304/radeap-A-control.log

$ tools/tb sudotool tb277 dot1x1304 eapol eth4 \
      --supplicant 02:0d:b9:00:33:54:cknotify:cknotifypw:success \
      --timeout 45 --debug --label T33354-A-CONTROL-no-notification \
      --pcap /tmp/dot1x1304/T33354-A.pcap --json /tmp/dot1x1304/T33354-A.json

eapol T33354-A-CONTROL-no-notification
  02:0d:b9:00:33:54  identity=cknotify     expect=success 
  filter: ether proto 0x888e   timeout: 45 s

