STEP B -- the server sends an EAP-Request/Notification                    PASS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Method: identical to STEP A except for one flag on the server.  Same server, same
  user, same supplicant MAC, same port.

$ tools/tb tool tb277 dot1x1304 radeap ... \
      --notify "ck-T33354 notification: password expires in 3 days" \
      --log /tmp/dot1x1304/radeap-B-notify.log

eapol T33354-B-WITH-EAP-Notification
  02:0d:b9:00:33:54  identity=cknotify     expect=success 
  filter: ether proto 0x888e   timeout: 45 s

pcap -> /tmp/dot1x1304/T33354-B.pcap (8 EAPOL frames)

     0.003 02:0d:b9:00:33:54 -> EAPOL-Start
     0.009 02:0d:b9:00:33:54 <- EAP-Request/Identity id=1 len=0 raw=
     0.014 02:0d:b9:00:33:54 -> EAP-Response/Identity "cknotify"
     0.021 02:0d:b9:00:33:54 <- EAP-Request/Notification id=2 len=50 raw=636b2d543333333534206e6f74696669636174696f6e3a2070617373776f7264206578706972657320696e20332064617973
     0.021 02:0d:b9:00:33:54    NOTIFICATION TEXT: 'ck-T33354 notification: password expires in 3 days'
     0.024 02:0d:b9:00:33:54 -> EAP-Response/Notification (empty, per RFC 3748 5.2)
     0.028 02:0d:b9:00:33:54 <- EAP-Request/MD5-Challenge id=3 len=17 raw=1005d9a91b28bed8ce1a7bb8c2bc1cec0a
     0.031 02:0d:b9:00:33:54 -> EAP-Response/MD5-Challenge digest=6b8d9691769174b079661b34ea0d44b1
